Serves as the IT Project Manager for the USAFRICOM J6 performing work independently or as a team lead for specific IT projects in the administration, development, delivery and support of information technology (IT) systems and services.
The incumbent is responsible for management and operational control over assigned IT projects following project management standards and established PM business practices and techniques in support of the USAFRICOM.
Duties include developing new methods, approaches and procedures in IT specialty area(s); providing advice and guidance on a wide range and variety of complex IT issues;
interpreting DoD IT policies, standards, and guidelines; developing drafts of USAFRICOM J6 IT policies, standards, and guidelines;
conducting analyses and recommending resolution of complex issues affecting operability of IT area(s); evaluating and recommending adoption of new or enhanced approaches to delivering IT services;
identifying and defining business or technical requirements applied to the design, development, implementation, management and support of systems and networks; ensuring optimal use of commercially available products;
evaluating proposals for the acquisition of IT products or services;
preparing and presenting reports; assisting the Deputy Chief Information Officer (DCIO) and the USAFRICOM J6 with interactions across other divisions and/or directorates when relating to the explanation of new technology;
and providing technical experience with existing or new IT technologies and services.

You will:
Design and implement IT system changes, and develop standard operating procedures for use;
Diagnose and resolve information and data related problems in response to customer related incidents;
Serve as Project Officer, Contracting Officer Representative (COR), or Contracting Officer's Technical Representative (COTR);
Provide customer support for problem solving, integrating and managing functional operations of multiple computer systems, software packages, networks and applications programs;
Develop outreach strategies and materials to communicate information about system changes.
When entering a Federal job at a grade level lower than the highest promotion potential level, you may be promoted to more complex duties and work more independently, as your career progresses.  NOTE:  Career ladder promotions are not automatic, and all eligibility and qualifications requirements must be met in order to progress to the next grade level.
You will spend less than 25% of your work time on contracts, grants/cooperative agreements, and/or interagency agreements.
One or more positions may be filled (in the organization advertised and/or in other organizations), if appropriate to the position.

Joining Customs & Border Protection will allow you to use your expertise in Information Technology principles, concepts and methods to support Information Technology systems and services. This position starts at a salary of $109,278.00 (GS-13, Step 1) to $142,065.00 (GS-13, Step 10) with promotion potential to $142,065.00 (GS-13 Step 10). Apply for this exciting opportunity to strengthen the Department's ability to perform homeland security functions by supervising technical and analytical work pertaining to the maintenance and development of Information Technology systems.
